// t_5c12df56 control: a HALF return that is not the colour.
//
// The entry returns half for the DEPTH export while an out parameter binds
// COLOR0 at fp32.  A COLOR0 store an out parameter owns belongs to that
// parameter whatever the entry returns, so this program's colour must stay
// in R0 at full precision with outputFromH0 clear - which is what the
// reference emits (colour word 0x1E000100, depth word 0x08030140, flag 0).
//
// A first draft of the half-return detection read "half return type AND a
// COLOR0 store exists" and turned this shader's fp32 colour into H0.
half main(out float4 colour : COLOR) : DEPTH
{
    colour = float4(0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0);
    return 0.5;
}
